prompt:
Use Three.js to implement a lantern festival scene. 20 lanterns slowly rise into the sky, each with a glowing point light inside, with support for day/night switching and click-to-change-color interaction.

[Three.js Import Method (Must Be Followed Strictly)]
Use the following importmap in <head>, and import via ES Modules in <script type="module">:
<script type="importmap">
{ "imports": {
    "three": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/three@0.170.0/build/three.module.js",
    "three/addons/": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/three@0.170.0/examples/jsm/"
} }
</script>
<script type="module">
import * as THREE from 'three';
import { GLTFLoader } from 'three/addons/loaders/GLTFLoader.js';
import { OrbitControls } from 'three/addons/controls/OrbitControls.js';
// Write your code here
</script>

[Model Loading]
(1) Use GLTFLoader to load assets/Lantern.glb;
(2) Create 20 cloned lanterns distributed at random positions (x: -15~15, y: 0~15, z: -15~15);
(3) Scale each lantern appropriately (approximately 0.5-0.8 random scale);
(4) After loading is complete, set window.__3D_STATE__.modelLoaded = true;

[Lantern Lighting Effects]
(5) Attach a PointLight at the internal center position of each lantern, with intensity 0.8 and decay distance 5;
(6) Each lantern's PointLight color must be a random warm color (randomly selected from the following presets: 0xff6600 orange, 0xff3300 red-orange, 0xffcc00 gold, 0xff9900 amber, 0xff4444 warm red);
(7) The PointLight intensity must have a subtle flickering effect (sinusoidal variation of ±0.2);

[Lantern Ascent Motion]
(8) All lanterns slowly float upward at a speed of 0.2 m/s;
(9) While rising, the lanterns must have subtle horizontal swaying (sinusoidal variation in the x and z directions, amplitude 0.3, with different frequencies for each);
(10) When a lantern's y-coordinate reaches 30, it must begin fading out: opacity transitions from 1 to 0 (completed in approximately 2 seconds);
(11) After becoming fully transparent, the lantern must respawn at the bottom (a random height of y=0~2), at a new random x/z position, with opacity restored to 1;
(12) Lantern materials must have transparent = true to support the fade-out effect;

[Click Interaction]
(13) Use Raycaster to detect mouse clicks on lanterns;
(14) After a lantern is clicked, randomly change its internal PointLight color to another warm color (select a color from the preset list that differs from the current color);
(15) The clicked lantern must briefly display an enlargement pulse effect (1.2 times its size, then return to normal);
(16) Record the index of the last clicked lantern;

[Day/Night Switching]
(17) A "Day/Night" toggle button (id="dayNightBtn");
(18) Day mode: sky blue 0x87CEEB, AmbientLight intensity 0.6, and a DirectionalLight simulating sunlight; lantern PointLight intensity reduced to 0.3 (not prominent during the day);
(19) Night mode: deep blue sky 0x0a0a2e, AmbientLight intensity 0.05, no DirectionalLight; lantern PointLight intensity 0.8 (highly prominent at night);
(20) Smoothly transition when switching (completed in approximately 1 second);

[Scene Setup]
(21) The ground must be a dark plane (0x1a1a1a), with an OrbitControls camera;
(22) In night mode, dynamic light and shadow cast by the lanterns must be visible on the ground;

[HUD Display]
(23) The HUD in the upper-left corner must display:
  - Total number of lanterns (id="lanternCount", must be 20)
  - Current time of day (id="timeOfDay", "day" or "night")
  - ID of the last clicked lantern (id="clickedLantern", -1 indicates that none has been clicked)
  - Average lantern height (id="avgHeight", rounded to 1 decimal place)

[State Exposure (Required)]
Update window.__3D_STATE__ every frame:
{
  modelLoaded: boolean,
  lanternCount: number,
  timeOfDay: string,
  clickedLanternId: number,
  avgHeight: number,
  lanternHeights: number[],
  dayNightTransitioning: boolean
}

Output a single HTML file placed in the same directory as the assets/ folder, and run it through a local HTTP server.
